## Give the application a home

A project groups related services and resources inside a workspace. Use a name that helps the next person recognize the application, then keep its persistent identifier in deployment records.

## Model environments explicitly

Development, staging and production have different jobs. Give each environment its own configuration and data bindings. A shared source repository does not require a shared production database.

## Keep the resource map readable

List the web service, worker, database and storage used by the application. A person should be able to inspect that map without reconstructing it from environment-variable names.

## Start small

Follow the [quickstart](/docs/quickstart), then read [services](/docs/services) and [data bindings](/docs/data).
